{"nodes": [{"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_stage_definition_format", "label": "Stage Definition Format (authoritative stage-file contract)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "YAML frontmatter is authoritative and the compiled JSON is generated from it, so the schema, the parser, and every stage file implement against one document rather than drifting into three conventions."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_mode_field", "label": "mode field (stage communication topology)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Authored fields, mode", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "agent-team is reserved and consumers must handle it explicitly (at minimum throwing not-implemented) rather than falling through to a default, because silent fallthrough on enum extension is a known foot-gun. The review loop is deliberately NOT a mode: reviewer plus reviewer_max_iterations deliver the two-party critique topology on top of every mode."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_engine_resolved_artifact_paths", "label": "Engine-resolved artifact paths (no stage file hardcodes a root)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Artifact paths are engine-resolved", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stage emits relative artifact names and the engine resolves them against the active intent's record dir at emit time, because a hardcoded workspace root would read false the moment the record re-roots per intent; the outputs: frontmatter is therefore non-load-bearing documentation and a rooted literal in a stage file is a doc bug, not a behaviour contract."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_consumes_absent", "label": "consumes_absent (absence-by-design arrives as data)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Artifact paths are engine-resolved", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Required inputs whose files are missing move to consumes_absent annotated expected true/false depending on whether the scope deliberately skipped the producer, and an absent optional consume is simply dropped, so the conductor is never pointed at an unreadable path and absence-by-design never surfaces as a failed read."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_compile_drift_invariant", "label": "Compile + drift invariant (aidlc-graph compile --check)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Compile + drift invariant", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CI re-runs the compile in memory and diffs against the checked-in JSON, so drift between the YAML sources and the compiled graph is impossible while the check passes."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_scope_grid", "label": "Scope membership grid (EXECUTE/SKIP transpose)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Authored fields, scopes", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each stage names the scopes it belongs to and the compile step transposes those declarations into the EXECUTE/SKIP grid, so scope membership is authored once per stage instead of maintained as a separate matrix that could disagree."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_reserved_namespace", "label": "Reserved field namespace (when, on_failure, blocks_on, timeout, retry)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Future extensions \u2014 reserved namespace", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Naming planned primitives before they exist prevents future contributor additions from colliding with them; blocks_on in particular is reserved to split today's overloaded requires_stage, which conflates 'I consume your output' with 'I run after you'."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_swarm_trigger_coupling", "label": "Swarm-trigger field coupling (for_each + mode)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Future extensions \u2014 reserved namespace", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The autonomous Construction swarm fires on a field match rather than an explicit flag, so re-moding the per-unit build stage silently takes it off the swarm path; the compiler emits an advisory on stderr precisely because the coupling is implicit."}], "edges": [{"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_conductor_communication_topologies", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_mode_field", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Authored fields, mode", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_stage_definition_format", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_stage_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Cross-references", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_stage_definition_format", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_mode_field", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Authored fields", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_stage_definition_format", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_engine_resolved_artifact_paths", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Artifact paths are engine-resolved", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_engine_resolved_artifact_paths", "target": "_claude_claude_intent_record_dir", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Artifact paths are engine-resolved", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_consumes_absent", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_engine_resolved_artifact_paths", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Artifact paths are engine-resolved", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_consumes_absent", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_scope_grid", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Artifact paths are engine-resolved (expected: true)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_compile_drift_invariant", "target": "_claude_claude_stage_graph", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Compile + drift invariant", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_compile_drift_invariant", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_scope_grid", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Authored fields, scopes", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_swarm_trigger_coupling", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_mode_field", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Swarm-trigger coupling", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_reserved_namespace", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_recovery_error_recovery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Future extensions (on_failure moves revision semantics out of stage-protocol-recovery.md)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_mode_field", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_reviewer_invocation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-definition.md", "source_location": "## Authored fields, mode (the review loop is NOT a mode)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_stages_construction_build_and_test_build_and_test", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_definition_stage_definition_format", "relation": "impl